                      Brute Force
class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            if (nums[i] == target) {
                return i;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
}

                    Intuition
The array is sorted but rotated, so a normal Binary Search cannot always determine which side is sorted.
Use a modified Binary Search:
Find the middle element.
If it is the target, return its index.
Check whether the left half is sorted (nums[left] <= nums[mid]).
If the target lies in this sorted half, search the left half.
Otherwise, search the right half.
Otherwise, the right half must be sorted.
If the target lies in the sorted right half, search the right half.
Otherwise, search the left half.

              Time Complexity
O(log n)
